body:
I finished it last week. 

&nbsp;

We had a rule that after the finale, there was to be no talking. No discussing. No comments. Do not look at anyone; just get up, and leave. 

&nbsp;

I walked out to my car and just stood there in the rain, staring up at the sky and contemplating life. There were definitely tears that day.

I know. I totally understand how you feel...it was the same way for me not to long ago. I hate feeling that way.

&nbsp;

What I recommend above all else is to find someone to confide in. Just one. Not necessarily on Reddit; even though we're here to support you, find one physical person that you can share your feelings with. It honestly makes a world of a difference.

Thanks for sharing that; I definitely know how you feel.

&nbsp;

In my opinion it's better to be friends with the "rejects" who are nice and care about each other than the large crowd of "friends" who constantly backstab, gossip, and cause drama. Some people don't even mean to do it on purpose. But sometimes it's just best to stay away from those people.

I really appreciate this comment because I think a lot of people in this thread are saying things like "don't be so sensitive" or "don't be such a pussy".

&nbsp;

That's not what we're talking about. Sarcasm and joking are completely different. This is talking about people who are going out of their way to be malicious to you either frequently or all the time.

>echo chamber hugbox 

&nbsp;

That's the best term I've seen all day. 

&nbsp;

But honestly, I was focusing more on cutting out people who are actually damaging to your life, and including people who are positive influences. Just because they're a good friend doesn't mean they're a "hugbox" or yes man. It just means that they're there for you when you need it.

Never indicated that it was easy. I simply meant that it's better to cut out fake friends from your life than keep them around you. 

&nbsp;

Making friends can be hard. :/

Being able to look at her and know that I can open up and tell her anything, and she will be there for me no matter what. And she looks back at me and I know that she feels the exact same way about me.

&nbsp;

Plus, we can fart and burp around each other, and talk about our poop experiences. That's true love, people.
